//! Mechanical parts: what is on the board and not in the circuit, or on one net by a screw,
//! and text on the silkscreen.
//!
//! None of these has a value to pick, so none has a catalog. A hole, a fiducial and a test
//! point are fitted by nobody, so each states `.assembly &= AssemblyMode::None` and is on no BOM and no
//! placement file (ADR 0024).
//!
//! These follow the recommendation of ADR 0020 (ADR 0023): `MountingHole` is non-plated with no
//! pins, `PlatedHole` has one pin that a screw bonds to a net or leaves open, `Fiducial` has no
//! pins, and `TestPoint` has one `required` pin. A part with no pins is on no net and is fitted by
//! nobody.
//!
//! A hole, a fiducial and a test point have no body: each states `.height &= 0mm`, a statement
//! ("flat") and not a default, so a height limit and the 3D coverage count them as known and not
//! as unknown. A board that gives one a height of its own contradicts it.
//!
//! Why parts (ADR 0020, decided by the owner on 2026-11-02): one mechanism for every footprint
//! on the board, with a reference designator, a footprint through the export mapping, a place
//! from the placer or the layout file, and a line in the schematic if it has a pin. The
//! language has no boolean, so a plated and a non-plated hole are two kinds and not a flag.
//! The placer treats a hole and a fiducial by kind and puts them in the corners of a fixed
//! outline. Rejected: features of the outline (`.outline.corner_holes &= 4`: short for the
//! common case, but holes elsewhere need a second way, and a plated hole with a net or a test
//! point cannot be an outline feature), and board members with coordinates in the source (a
//! second place for a position beside the layout file). The checks name numbers: a drill
//! below `process.min_drill`, a plated hole whose pad leaves less than `min_annular_ring`, a
//! hole nearer the edge than `min_edge_clearance`.
//!
//! Silkscreen. The text no smaller than the process allows and none over a pad or the board
//! edge are the placer's and the design rules check's job. A `Label` is a part with no pins,
//! with its text as a string and its size a range (the least wins, never below the process's
//! least text), with a footprint generated from the text, reference `LBL1` and no symbol.
//! Rejected: a board-level `text "REV A" at ...` statement (it needs coordinates in the
//! source) and derived text such as a net name beside each connector pad (derivable with no
//! statement, but a board might want it off, so it would be a switch on the connector).
//! Logos are not built.
//!
//! Assembly is the part's field: what is always true of a kind is stated by the library (a
//! hole, a fiducial and a label are never fitted), what a fab cannot place is a column of the
//! catalog row, and whether this instance is hand-soldered or not fitted is the design's
//! (ADR 0024, ADR 0028). A part marked `none` stays in the electrical model, so the solver
//! and the balance still count it, which is conservative for a supply. Assembly variants are
//! not built.

/// A mounting hole with no copper: a drill for a screw that touches no net. It has no pins,
/// so it is on no net.
part MountingHole {
    .designator &= "H"
    .height &= 0mm
    .assembly &= AssemblyMode::None
    .package: Package
}

/// A mounting hole plated through, with a pad that a screw bonds to a net (the chassis, or
/// ground). Its one pin `p1` is the plating: the board joins it to a net, or leaves it open
/// for a hole whose pad floats.
part PlatedHole {
    .designator &= "H"

    pins {
        .p1 passive "1" "1"
    }

    .assembly &= AssemblyMode::None
    .package: Package
}

/// A fiducial: a bare copper mark that the pick-and-place machine locates the board by. It
/// has no pins, so it is on no net.
part Fiducial {
    .designator &= "FID"
    .height &= 0mm
    .assembly &= AssemblyMode::None
    .package: Package
}

/// A test point: one pad on a net, to touch with a probe. Its pin `p1` is `required`, because
/// a test point on no net tests nothing.
part TestPoint {
    .designator &= "TP"
    .height &= 0mm

    pins {
        .p1 passive "TP" "1" required
    }

    .assembly &= AssemblyMode::None
    .package: Package
}

/// A line of text printed on the silkscreen: a revision, a name, a polarity mark. It has no
/// pins, is fitted by nobody, and is placed like any other part. Its `.text_height` is at least the
/// process's smallest text; unset, it is that.
part Label {
    .designator &= "LBL"
    .assembly &= AssemblyMode::None
    .text: String
    .text_height: Length
}
